course: dictionary
lesson: 3530
title: Feast: a meal, a treat, or a verb
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A feast is a large, special meal with lots of food, often for a celebration. A feast can also be a religious festival day. Context helps you choose: «For Orthodox Christians Easter is the greatest feast» means a special holy day, not a dinner.
explain: Feast can be a verb too, meaning to eat a lot of good food with enjoyment. Look at the words around it. In «gulls and swifts feast on them», the birds are doing something, so feast is a verb. In «many men were feasting in his hall, eating his food», the words eating and food show the meaning is eating with enjoyment.
explain: Feast can also mean something lovely to look at, as in «a feast for the eyes». Try the swap test: put «something lovely to look at» in place of «a feast for the eyes». If the sentence still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
fact: A feast is a large, special meal with lots of food, often for a celebration.
fact: As a noun, feast can also mean a religious festival day, like Easter for some Christians.
fact: As a verb, to feast means to eat a lot of good food with enjoyment, as in «feast on».
fact: «Feast your eyes on» means look at something with pleasure.
fact: A «midnight feast» is a secret snack party, popular in school stories.
exercise: «When Odysseus got home, many men were feasting in his hall, eating his food.» What does feasting mean here? | Singing in a choir | Sleeping quietly in bed | Running away from danger | *Eating a lot of good food with enjoyment
exercise: In «gulls and swifts feast on them», what kind of word is feast? | Adjective, a describing word | Noun, a naming word | *Verb, an action word | Full stop
exercise: Ayo says «a feast for the eyes» means a huge dinner. What does it really mean? | Something cold to eat | A kind of bird | *Something lovely to look at | A very big dinner for the whole family
test: «For Orthodox Christians Easter is the greatest feast.» What does feast mean in this sentence? | *A religious festival day | A small snack | A secret snack party | Eating with enjoyment
test: Which phrase means look at something with pleasure? | Feast on berries | *Feast your eyes on | Midnight feast | Feast of fools
exam: In a school story, what does «a midnight feast» mean? | A religious festival day | *A secret snack party | A boring lesson | A weekly shopping trip
